[2026-03-14T21:02:51.054Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015GoLUP1VcE9pNCyiwp1q84","type":"tool_result","content":"   500→\n   501→#### Test: Inbox page shows empty state when no notifications\n   502→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has no notifications\n   503→- **Expected**: The page displays a friendly empty state message with an icon (e.g., \"No notifications yet\" or \"You're all caught up!\") instead of an empty list.\n   504→\n   505→#### Test: Inbox shows unread notifications visually distinct from read\n   506→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has 2 unread notifications and 1 read notification\n   507→- **Expected**: Unread notifications appear with bold text and a left border accent (using the primary accent color `#5e6ad2`). Read notifications appear with normal weight text and no left border accent.\n   508→\n   509→#### Test: Inbox page shows notification count in header\n   510→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has 5 unread notifications\n   511→- **Expected**: The inbox header or a badge near it indicates the number of unread notifications (e.g., \"Inbox (5)\" or a count badge).\n   512→\n   513→#### Test: Inbox notification list updates sidebar badge when notifications change\n   514→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has 3 unread notifications, sidebar Inbox badge shows \"3\"\n   515→- **Action**: User marks one notification as read on the inbox page\n   516→- **Expected**: The sidebar Inbox badge updates to \"2\".\n   517→\n   518→#### Test: Inbox notifications are ordered by newest first\n   519→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has notifications from 5 minutes ago, 1 hour ago, and 1 day ago\n   520→- **Expected**: Notifications appear in order: 5 minutes ago (top), 1 hour ago (middle), 1 day ago (bottom).\n   521→\n   522→#### Test: Archiving a notification removes it from the list\n   523→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has 3 notifications visible in the inbox\n   524→- **Action**: User clicks the archive button/icon on the first notification\n   525→- **Expected**: The notification is removed from the inbox list. The list now shows 2 notifications. The archived notification does not reappear.\n   526→\n   527→#### Test: Archiving multiple notifications works in sequence\n   528→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has 3 notifications visible\n   529→- **Action**: User archives the first notification, then archives what is now the first notification\n   530→- **Expected**: Both notifications are removed. The list shows 1 remaining notification. The archive action works correctly on repeated use.\n   531→\n   532→#### Test: All notifications can be archived to reach empty state\n   533→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has 2 notifications visible\n   534→- **Action**: User archives both notifications one by one\n   535→- **Expected**: After all notifications are archived, the empty state message is displayed. The sidebar Inbox badge disappears (no unread count).\n   536→\n   537→### NotificationRow\n   538→\n   539→#### Test: Notification row displays assignment notification correctly\n   540→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has a notification for \"Issue ENG-42 was assigned to you\" created 5 minutes ago\n   541→- **Expected**: The notification row displays: an assignment-type icon (e.g., user-plus or assign icon), issue identifier \"ENG-42\", description text \"assigned to you\" or similar, and relative timestamp \"5m ago\". The row is visually complete and well-formatted.\n   542→\n   543→#### Test: Notification row displays issue update notification correctly\n   544→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has a notification for \"Issue ENG-15 status changed to Done\" on a subscribed issue, created 1 hour ago\n   545→- **Expected**: The notification row displays: an update-type icon (e.g., refresh or edit icon), issue identifier \"ENG-15\", description \"status changed to Done\" or similar, and relative timestamp \"1h ago\".\n   546→\n   547→#### Test: Notification row displays mention notification correctly\n   548→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has a notification for \"You were mentioned in a comment on ENG-7\" created 2 hours ago\n   549→- **Expected**: The notification row displays: a mention-type icon (e.g., at-sign icon), issue identifier \"ENG-7\", description \"mentioned you in a comment\" or similar, and relative timestamp \"2h ago\".\n   550→\n   551→#### Test: Clicking an unread notification marks it as read\n   552→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has an unread notification for issue ENG-42 (bold text, left border accent)\n   553→- **Action**: User clicks on the notification row\n   554→- **Expected**: The notification's visual style changes from unread (bold, left border accent) to read (normal weight, no left border accent). The change is persisted to the database. The sidebar Inbox badge count decrements by 1.\n   555→\n   556→#### Test: Clicking a read notification does not change its state\n   557→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has a read notification (normal weight, no accent)\n   558→- **Action**: User clicks on the notification row\n   559→- **Expected**: The notification remains in its read visual state. No redundant database update is made.\n   560→\n   561→#### Test: Clicking a notification navigates to the related issue\n   562→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has a notification for issue ENG-42\n   563→- **Action**: User clicks on the notification row\n   564→- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/issue/<issueId>` for issue ENG-42. The issue detail page loads showing ENG-42.\n   565→\n   566→#### Test: Notification row archive button is visible\n   567→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has a notification visible in the inbox\n   568→- **Expected**: Each notification row has an archive button/icon (e.g., an archive or x icon) visible on hover or always visible, allowing the user to archive the notification.\n   569→\n   570→#### Test: Notification row archive button archives without navigating\n   571→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing the inbox with a notification for ENG-42\n   572→- **Action**: User clicks the archive button on the ENG-42 notification row\n   573→- **Expected**: The notification is archived and removed from the list. The user remains on the `/inbox` page — no navigation to the issue detail occurs. The archive action is persisted to the database.\n   574→\n   575→#### Test: Notification row shows correct icon per notification type\n   576→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has one of each notification type: assignment, issue update, mention\n   577→- **Expected**: Each notification type has a distinct, recognizable icon: assignment uses a user/assign icon, issue update uses a refresh/change icon, mention uses an at-sign/@-symbol icon. The icons are visually differentiated by shape or style.\n   578→\n   579→#### Test: Notification row displays relative timestamps that update\n   580→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has a notification created \"just now\"\n   581→- **Expected**: The timestamp shows \"just now\" or \"1m ago\" (relative format). Timestamps use relative format throughout (e.g., \"5m ago\", \"1h ago\", \"2d ago\") rather than absolute dates.\n   582→\n   583→#### Test: Marking notification as read then archiving works correctly\n   584→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has an unread notification for ENG-42\n   585→- **Action**: User clicks the notification to mark as read, then clicks the archive button on the same notification\n   586→- **Expected**: The notification is first marked as read (visual change), then archived and removed from the list. Both actions succeed in sequence without conflict.\n   587→\n   588→#### Test: Notification row click and archive button have separate hit targets\n   589→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has a notification in the inbox\n   590→- **Action**: User clicks specifically on the archive button area of a notification row\n   591→- **Expected**: Only the archive action fires — the notification is archived. The user does NOT navigate to the issue detail page. The click targets for \"mark as read + navigate\" and \"archive\" are clearly separated.\n   592→\n   593→## Team Issues Page (`/team/:teamId/issues`)\n   594→\n   595→**Components**: TeamIssuesList, BulkActions, GroupBySort, TeamFilters\n   596→\n   597→### TeamIssuesList\n   598→\n   599→#### Test: Team Issues page renders with header showing team name\n   600→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, navigates to `/team/eng-1/issues` for team \"Engineering\"\n   601→- **Expected**: The page displays a header with the team name \"Engineering\" and an \"Issues\" label. A \"New Issue\" button is visible in the header area.\n   602→\n   603→#### Test: Team Issues page shows issues grouped by status (default)\n   604→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, \"Engineering\" team has issues in Backlog (3), In Progress (2), Done (1)\n   605→- **Expected**: Issues are grouped under status headers. Each group header shows the status icon, status name, and issue count in parentheses. Groups appear in status order: Backlog, Todo, In Progress, In Review, Done, Cancelled. Empty status groups are not displayed.\n   606→\n   607→#### Test: Team Issues page shows all team issues, not just current user's\n   608→- **Initial state**: User \"Alice\" is authenticated, \"Engineering\" team has issues: ENG-1 (assigned to Alice), ENG-2 (assigned to Bob), ENG-3 (unassigned)\n   609→- **Expected**: All three issues (ENG-1, ENG-2, ENG-3) are visible on the team issues page.\n   610→\n   611→#### Test: Team Issues page shows empty state when team has no issues\n   612→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, \"Engineering\" team has no issues\n   613→- **Expected**: A friendly empty state message with an icon is displayed (e.g., \"No issues yet. Create your first issue to get started.\") and the \"New Issue\" button is visible.\n   614→\n   615→#### Test: Issue row displays all required fields including checkbox and team prefix\n   616→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues. Issue ENG-42 exists with title \"Fix login bug\", status \"In Progress\", priority \"High\", labels [\"Bug\"], assignee \"Jane Doe\" (with avatar), due date \"2026-03-20\", project \"Auth Rewrite\".\n   617→- **Expected**: The issue row displays: a checkbox for bulk selection (unchecked), High priority icon (orange arrow-up), identifier \"ENG-42\" with team prefix, title \"Fix login bug\", In Progress status icon (yellow half circle), \"Bug\" label as a small colored badge, assignee avatar, due date \"Mar 20\", and project name \"Auth Rewrite\".\n   618→\n   619→#### Test: Issue row title is clickable and navigates to issue detail\n   620→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues with issue ENG-42\n   621→- **Action**: User clicks on the title \"Fix login bug\" in the issue row\n   622→- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/issue/<issueId>` for issue ENG-42.\n   623→\n   624→#### Test: Issue row status icon is clickable to change status\n   625→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues. Issue ENG-42 has status \"Todo\".\n   626→- **Action**: User clicks the status icon on the ENG-42 issue row\n   627→- **Expected**: A dropdown/popover appears showing all available statuses (Backlog, Todo, In Progress, In Review, Done, Cancelled) with their respective icons and colors.\n   628→\n   629→#### Test: Changing status via issue row status dropdown persists and moves issue between groups\n   630→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues grouped by status. \"Todo\" group has ENG-42. \"In Progress\" group has 1 issue.\n   631→- **Action**: User clicks the status icon on ENG-42, selects \"In Progress\" from the dropdown\n   632→- **Expected**: The dropdown closes. ENG-42 moves from the \"Todo\" group to the \"In Progress\" group. Group counts update accordingly. The change is persisted to the database.\n   633→\n   634→#### Test: Issue row status dropdown can be used multiple times\n   635→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, issue ENG-42 has status \"Todo\"\n   636→- **Action**: User clicks status icon, changes to \"In Progress\", then clicks status icon again, changes to \"Done\"\n   637→- **Expected**: Both status changes work correctly. The issue ends up in the \"Done\" group with a green check circle icon. Each dropdown opens and closes cleanly.\n   638→\n   639→#### Test: Status group headers are collapsible\n   640→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, \"In Progress\" group is expanded with 2 issues\n   641→- **Action**: User clicks the \"In Progress\" group header\n   642→- **Expected**: The group collapses, hiding all issues within it. The group header remains visible with a collapse indicator (e.g., chevron rotates). Clicking again expands the group back.\n   643→\n   644→#### Test: Status group collapse toggles multiple times\n   645→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, \"Backlog\" group is expanded with 3 issues\n   646→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Backlog\" header to collapse, clicks it again to expand, then collapses once more\n   647→- **Expected**: Each click toggles correctly. After three clicks, the group is collapsed and its issues are hidden. The count in parentheses remains accurate.\n   648→\n   649→#### Test: Multiple status groups can be independently collapsed\n   650→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has issues in Backlog, In Progress, and Done groups, all expanded\n   651→- **Action**: User collapses the \"Backlog\" group, then collapses the \"Done\" group\n   652→- **Expected**: \"Backlog\" and \"Done\" groups are collapsed while \"In Progress\" remains expanded showing its issues.\n   653→\n   654→#### Test: Issue row displays priority icon with correct color\n   655→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues with issues at different priorities\n   656→- **Expected**: Urgent shows red alert-triangle icon, High shows orange arrow-up, Medium shows yellow minus, Low shows blue arrow-down, No Priority shows gray dots-horizontal.\n   657→\n   658→#### Test: Issue row displays labels as colored badges\n   659→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, issue ENG-42 has labels \"Bug\" (red) and \"Frontend\" (blue)\n   660→- **Expected**: Both labels are shown as small colored badges in the issue row, each with the label's color and name text.\n   661→\n   662→#### Test: Issue row shows assignee avatar\n   663→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, issue ENG-42 is assigned to \"Jane Doe\" who has an avatar\n   664→- **Expected**: The issue row shows Jane Doe's avatar as a small circular image. If no avatar, shows initials.\n   665→\n   666→#### Test: Issue row hides optional fields when not set\n   667→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, issue ENG-43 has no labels, no due date, no project, no assignee\n   668→- **Expected**: The issue row does not show empty placeholders for labels, due date, project, or assignee. Only the present fields (checkbox, priority, identifier, title, status) are shown.\n   669→\n   670→#### Test: New Issue button opens create issue modal with team pre-selected\n   671→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing `/team/eng-1/issues` for team \"Engineering\"\n   672→- **Action**: User clicks the \"New Issue\" button\n   673→- **Expected**: The create issue modal opens with the team selector pre-set to \"Engineering\". The title field is focused.\n   674→\n   675→#### Test: New Issue button text and icon appearance\n   676→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues page\n   677→- **Expected**: The \"New Issue\" button is visible with text \"New Issue\" and displays appropriately (e.g., with a plus icon). The button uses the primary accent style.\n   678→\n   679→#### Test: Newly created issue appears in the list\n   680→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues for \"Engineering\" with 3 issues\n   681→- **Action**: User clicks \"New Issue\", fills in the title \"New feature request\" with status \"Backlog\", and submits the form\n   682→- **Expected**: The modal closes. The new issue appears in the \"Backlog\" group with the next sequential identifier (e.g., ENG-44). The group count updates.\n   683→\n   684→### BulkActions\n   685→\n   686→#### Test: Issue row checkboxes are visible and unchecked by default\n   687→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues with 5 issues\n   688→- **Expected**: Each issue row has a checkbox on the left side. All checkboxes are unchecked by default.\n   689→\n   690→#### Test: Clicking a checkbox selects an issue\n   691→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues with ENG-42 unchecked\n   692→- **Action**: User clicks the checkbox on ENG-42\n   693→- **Expected**: The checkbox becomes checked. The issue row has a selected visual style (e.g., highlighted background). A bulk action toolbar appears at the top or bottom of the list.\n   694→\n   695→#### Test: Clicking a checked checkbox deselects the issue\n   696→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, ENG-42 checkbox is checked, bulk action toolbar is visible\n   697→- **Action**: User clicks the checkbox on ENG-42 again\n   698→- **Expected**: The checkbox becomes unchecked. The selected visual style is removed from the row. If no other issues are selected, the bulk action toolbar disappears.\n   699→\n   700→#### Test: Multiple issues can be selected via checkboxes\n   701→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues with ENG-42, ENG-43, ENG-44\n   702→- **Action**: User clicks checkboxes on ENG-42 and ENG-44\n   703→- **Expected**: Both ENG-42 and ENG-44 are checked with selected visual style. ENG-43 remains unchecked. The bulk action toolbar shows \"2 selected\" or similar count indicator.\n   704→\n   705→#### Test: Bulk action toolbar appears when issues are selected\n   706→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, no issues selected, no bulk action toolbar visible\n   707→- **Action**: User clicks the checkbox on ENG-42\n   708→- **Expected**: A bulk action toolbar appears showing the selection count (\"1 selected\") and action buttons for: Status change, Priority change, Assignee change, and Label change.\n   709→\n   710→#### Test: Bulk action toolbar disappears when all issues are deselected\n   711→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, ENG-42 is selected, bulk action toolbar is visible\n   712→- **Action**: User unchecks ENG-42\n   713→- **Expected**: The bulk action toolbar disappears. No action buttons are visible.\n   714→\n   715→#### Test: Bulk status change updates all selected issues\n   716→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, ENG-42 (status \"Todo\") and ENG-43 (status \"Backlog\") are selected via checkboxes\n   717→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Status\" action in the bulk toolbar, selects \"In Progress\" from the dropdown\n   718→- **Expected**: Both ENG-42 and ENG-43 are updated to \"In Progress\" status. They move to the \"In Progress\" group. The changes are persisted to the database. The checkboxes are deselected and the bulk toolbar disappears.\n   719→\n   720→#### Test: Bulk priority change updates all selected issues\n   721→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, ENG-42 (priority \"Low\") and ENG-43 (priority \"Medium\") are selected\n   722→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Priority\" action in the bulk toolbar, selects \"High\" from the dropdown\n   723→- **Expected**: Both issues are updated to \"High\" priority. The priority icons change to orange arrow-up on both rows. Changes are persisted to the database.\n   724→\n   725→#### Test: Bulk assignee change updates all selected issues\n   726→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, ENG-42 (assigned to Alice) and ENG-43 (unassigned) are selected\n   727→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Assignee\" action in the bulk toolbar, selects \"Bob\" from the member selector\n   728→- **Expected**: Both issues are now assigned to Bob. The assignee avatars update on both rows. Changes are persisted to the database.\n   729→\n   730→#### Test: Bulk label change updates all selected issues\n   731→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, ENG-42 (no labels) and ENG-43 (label \"Bug\") are selected\n   732→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Label\" action in the bulk toolbar, selects \"Feature\" from the label picker\n   733→- **Expected**: Both issues now have the \"Feature\" label. ENG-43 retains its existing \"Bug\" label and also gains \"Feature\". Label badges update on both rows. Changes are persisted.\n   734→\n   735→#### Test: Bulk actions can be performed multiple times in sequence\n   736→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues with multiple issues\n   737→- **Action**: User selects ENG-42 and ENG-43, bulk-changes status to \"In Progress\", then selects ENG-44 and ENG-45, bulk-changes priority to \"High\"\n   738→- **Expected**: Both bulk actions complete successfully. The first pair is in \"In Progress\" status, the second pair has \"High\" priority. The bulk toolbar appears and disappears correctly each time.\n   739→\n   740→#### Test: Select all checkbox in group header selects all issues in that group\n   741→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, \"Backlog\" group has 3 issues, none selected\n   742→- **Action**: User clicks a \"select all\" checkbox in the \"Backlog\" group header\n   743→- **Expected**: All 3 issues in the Backlog group are selected (checkboxes checked, selected visual style). The bulk toolbar shows \"3 selected\". Issues in other groups remain unselected.\n   744→\n   745→#### Test: Deselect all via group header checkbox\n   746→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, all 3 issues in \"Backlog\" group are selected via group header checkbox\n   747→- **Action**: User clicks the group header checkbox again\n   748→- **Expected**: All 3 issues are deselected. If no other issues are selected, the bulk toolbar disappears.\n   749→\n   750→### GroupBySort\n   751→\n   752→#### Test: Group by control renders with default \"Status\" selected\n   753→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues page\n   754→- **Expected**: A \"Group by\" control/dropdown is visible in the toolbar area. It shows \"Status\" as the currently selected grouping option.\n   755→\n   756→#### Test: Group by dropdown shows all grouping options\n   757→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues page\n   758→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Group by\" control\n   759→- **Expected**: A dropdown opens showing options: Status, Priority, Assignee, Project, Label, None. Each option is clickable.\n   760→\n   761→#### Test: Group by Priority groups issues under priority headers\n   762→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues with priorities: Urgent (1), High (2), Medium (1), Low (1), No Priority (1)\n   763→- **Action**: User selects \"Priority\" from the Group by dropdown\n   764→- **Expected**: Issues are regrouped under priority headers: Urgent, High, Medium, Low, No Priority. Each header shows the priority icon, name, and count. Empty priority groups are not shown.\n   765→\n   766→#### Test: Group by Assignee groups issues under assignee headers\n   767→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues assigned to Alice (2), Bob (1), and unassigned (1)\n   768→- **Action**: User selects \"Assignee\" from the Group by dropdown\n   769→- **Expected**: Issues are grouped under assignee name headers with their avatars. An \"Unassigned\" group shows issues with no assignee. Each header shows the assignee avatar, name, and issue count.\n   770→\n   771→#### Test: Group by Project groups issues under project headers\n   772→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues in project \"Auth Rewrite\" (2), \"Dashboard v2\" (1), and no project (1)\n   773→- **Action**: User selects \"Project\" from the Group by dropdown\n   774→- **Expected**: Issues are grouped under project name headers. A \"No Project\" group shows unassigned issues. Each header shows the project name and issue count.\n   775→\n   776→#### Test: Group by Label groups issues under label headers\n   777→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues with labels \"Bug\" (2), \"Feature\" (1), and no labels (1)\n   778→- **Action**: User selects \"Label\" from the Group by dropdown\n   779→- **Expected**: Issues are grouped under label name headers with colored dots. A \"No Label\" group shows unlabeled issues. Issues with multiple labels appear under each applicable label group.\n   780→\n   781→#### Test: Group by None shows a flat list\n   782→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has 6 issues in various statuses\n   783→- **Action**: User selects \"None\" from the Group by dropdown\n   784→- **Expected**: All issues are displayed in a flat list without any group headers. Issues are shown in the current sort order.\n   785→\n   786→#### Test: Switching group by option re-renders immediately\n   787→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, issues are grouped by Status\n   788→- **Action**: User changes Group by from \"Status\" to \"Priority\"\n   789→- **Expected**: The issue list immediately re-renders with priority-based grouping. No page reload is needed. The transition is smooth.\n   790→\n   791→#### Test: Group by can be changed multiple times\n   792→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues\n   793→- **Action**: User selects \"Priority\" grouping, then \"Assignee\", then back to \"Status\"\n   794→- **Expected**: Each change correctly re-groups the issues. After returning to \"Status\", the view matches the original default grouping.\n   795→\n   796→#### Test: Sort by control renders with default option\n   797→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues page\n   798→- **Expected**: A \"Sort by\" control/dropdown is visible in the toolbar area, showing the current sort option.\n   799→\n   800→#### Test: Sort by dropdown shows all sorting options\n   801→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues page\n   802→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Sort by\" control\n   803→- **Expected**: A dropdown opens showing options: Priority, Created date, Updated date, Status. Each option is clickable.\n   804→\n   805→#### Test: Sort by Priority orders issues by priority level\n   806→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues with mixed priorities within status groups\n   807→- **Action**: User selects \"Priority\" from the Sort by dropdown\n   808→- **Expected**: Within each group, issues are ordered by priority: Urgent first, then High, Medium, Low, No Priority last.\n   809→\n   810→#### Test: Sort by Created date orders issues by creation time\n   811→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues created at different times\n   812→- **Action**: User selects \"Created date\" from the Sort by dropdown\n   813→- **Expected**: Within each group, issues are ordered by creation date (newest first).\n   814→\n   815→#### Test: Sort by Updated date orders issues by last update time\n   816→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues updated at different times\n   817→- **Action**: User selects \"Updated date\" from the Sort by dropdown\n   818→- **Expected**: Within each group, issues are ordered by last update time (most recently updated first).\n   819→\n   820→#### Test: Sort by Status orders issues by status progression\n   821→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, group by is set to \"None\" (flat list)\n   822→- **Action**: User selects \"Status\" from the Sort by dropdown\n   823→- **Expected**: Issues are ordered by status progression: Backlog, Todo, In Progress, In Review, Done, Cancelled.\n   824→\n   825→#### Test: Sort works correctly within groups\n   826→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, grouped by Status, \"In Progress\" group has 3 issues with different priorities\n   827→- **Action**: User selects \"Priority\" from Sort by\n   828→- **Expected**: The 3 issues within the \"In Progress\" group are reordered by priority (Urgent first, No Priority last). Other groups are similarly sorted.\n   829→\n   830→#### Test: Sort by can be changed multiple times\n   831→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues\n   832→- **Action**: User sorts by \"Priority\", then by \"Created date\", then by \"Updated date\"\n   833→- **Expected**: Each sort change correctly reorders issues within their groups. The sort control updates to reflect the current selection.\n   834→\n   835→### TeamFilters\n   836→\n   837→#### Test: Team filters toolbar renders with all filter options\n   838→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing `/team/eng-1/issues`\n   839→- **Expected**: A toolbar at the top of the issue list displays filter controls: \"Status\", \"Priority\", \"Assignee\", \"Label\", \"Project\", and \"Cycle\" filters. Each shows as a button/chip that can be clicked to open a dropdown.\n   840→\n   841→#### Test: Status filter dropdown shows all statuses with icons\n   842→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues\n   843→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Status\" filter button\n   844→- **Expected**: A multi-select dropdown opens showing all statuses: Backlog (dotted circle, gray), Todo (circle, gray), In Progress (half circle, yellow), In Review (three-quarter circle, blue), Done (check circle, green), Cancelled (x-circle, red). Each option has a checkbox.\n   845→\n   846→#### Test: Status filter filters issues by selected statuses\n   847→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues in Backlog (3), In Progress (2), Done (1)\n   848→- **Action**: User opens the Status filter and selects only \"In Progress\"\n   849→- **Expected**: Only the \"In Progress\" group is displayed with its 2 issues. Backlog and Done groups are hidden. The Status filter button shows a visual indicator that a filter is active.\n   850→\n   851→#### Test: Priority filter dropdown shows all priorities with icons\n   852→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues\n   853→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Priority\" filter button\n   854→- **Expected**: A multi-select dropdown opens showing: Urgent (alert-triangle, red), High (arrow-up, orange), Medium (minus, yellow), Low (arrow-down, blue), No Priority (dots-horizontal, gray). Each option has a checkbox.\n   855→\n   856→#### Test: Priority filter filters issues by selected priorities\n   857→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues with priorities High (2), Medium (1), Low (1)\n   858→- **Action**: User opens Priority filter and selects \"High\"\n   859→- **Expected**: Only issues with High priority are displayed across all status groups. Issues with Medium and Low priority are hidden.\n   860→\n   861→#### Test: Assignee filter dropdown shows all team members\n   862→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team \"Engineering\" has members Alice, Bob, and Charlie\n   863→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Assignee\" filter button\n   864→- **Expected**: A multi-select dropdown opens showing all team members with their avatars and names: Alice, Bob, Charlie, and an \"Unassigned\" option. Each option has a checkbox.\n   865→\n   866→#### Test: Assignee filter filters issues by selected assignees\n   867→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues: ENG-1 (Alice), ENG-2 (Bob), ENG-3 (Alice), ENG-4 (unassigned)\n   868→- **Action**: User opens Assignee filter and selects \"Alice\"\n   869→- **Expected**: Only issues assigned to Alice are shown (ENG-1 and ENG-3). Issues assigned to Bob and unassigned issues are hidden.\n   870→\n   871→#### Test: Label filter dropdown shows all available labels\n   872→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, workspace has labels \"Bug\" (red), \"Feature\" (green), \"Improvement\" (blue)\n   873→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Label\" filter button\n   874→- **Expected**: A multi-select dropdown opens showing all workspace labels with their colored dots and names. Each option has a checkbox.\n   875→\n   876→#### Test: Label filter filters issues by selected labels\n   877→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues: ENG-1 (labeled \"Bug\"), ENG-2 (labeled \"Feature\"), ENG-3 (labeled \"Bug\", \"Feature\")\n   878→- **Action**: User opens Label filter and selects \"Bug\"\n   879→- **Expected**: Only issues with the \"Bug\" label are shown (ENG-1 and ENG-3). ENG-2 is hidden.\n   880→\n   881→#### Test: Project filter dropdown shows all team projects\n   882→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has projects \"Auth Rewrite\" and \"Dashboard v2\"\n   883→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Project\" filter button\n   884→- **Expected**: A multi-select dropdown opens showing \"Auth Rewrite\", \"Dashboard v2\", and a \"No Project\" option. Each has a checkbox.\n   885→\n   886→#### Test: Project filter filters issues by selected projects\n   887→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues: ENG-1 (project \"Auth Rewrite\"), ENG-2 (project \"Dashboard v2\"), ENG-3 (no project)\n   888→- **Action**: User opens Project filter and selects \"Auth Rewrite\"\n   889→- **Expected**: Only ENG-1 is shown. ENG-2 and ENG-3 are hidden.\n   890→\n   891→#### Test: Cycle filter dropdown shows team cycles\n   892→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has cycles \"Sprint 1\" (active), \"Sprint 2\" (upcoming)\n   893→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Cycle\" filter button\n   894→- **Expected**: A multi-select dropdown opens showing \"Sprint 1\", \"Sprint 2\", and a \"No Cycle\" option. The active cycle is visually indicated. Each option has a checkbox.\n   895→\n   896→#### Test: Cycle filter filters issues by selected cycle\n   897→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues: ENG-1 (in \"Sprint 1\"), ENG-2 (in \"Sprint 1\"), ENG-3 (no cycle)\n   898→- **Action**: User opens Cycle filter and selects \"Sprint 1\"\n   899→- **Expected**: Only issues in Sprint 1 are shown (ENG-1 and ENG-2). ENG-3 is hidden.\n   900→\n   901→#### Test: Multiple filters combine with AND logic\n   902→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues: ENG-1 (High priority, Bug label, In Progress), ENG-2 (High priority, Feature label, In Progress), ENG-3 (Low priority, Bug label, Backlog)\n   903→- **Action**: User selects \"High\" in Priority filter and \"Bug\" in Label filter\n   904→- **Expected**: Only ENG-1 is shown (matches both High priority AND Bug label). ENG-2 and ENG-3 are hidden.\n   905→\n   906→#### Test: Clearing a filter restores all issues\n   907→- **Initial state**: User has Status filter set to \"In Progress\" only, showing 2 issues out of 6 total\n   908→- **Action**: User opens Status filter and deselects \"In Progress\" (or clicks a \"Clear\" option)\n   909→- **Expected**: All 6 issues are shown again across all status groups, same as the unfiltered view.\n   910→\n   911→#### Test: Filter state shows active filter indicators\n   912→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, no filters applied\n   913→- **Action**: User selects \"High\" in Priority filter\n   914→- **Expected**: The Priority filter button shows a visual indicator that it is active (e.g., highlighted background, badge showing \"1\", or different styling). Other filter buttons remain in their default/inactive state.\n   915→\n   916→#### Test: Filters can be used repeatedly after clearing\n   917→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated with multiple issues at various statuses and priorities\n   918→- **Action**: User applies Priority filter for \"High\", clears it, then applies Assignee filter for \"Alice\", clears it, then applies Status filter for \"Done\"\n   919→- **Expected**: Each filter application and clearing works correctly. After the final action, only \"Done\" issues are shown. All filter controls remain responsive and functional through multiple interactions.\n   920→\n   921→#### Test: Filters work correctly with grouping options\n   922→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, issues grouped by Priority, Assignee filter set to \"Alice\"\n   923→- **Expected**: Only Alice's issues are shown, grouped under their respective priority headers. Empty priority groups (where Alice has no issues) are not displayed.\n   924→\n   925→#### Test: Filters persist while navigating within the page\n   926→- **Initial state**: User has Status filter set to \"In Progress\", viewing filtered results\n   927→- **Action**: User clicks an issue title to view detail, then navigates back to `/team/eng-1/issues`\n   928→- **Expected**: The filters are still applied showing only \"In Progress\" issues. The filter state is preserved across navigation.\n   929→\n   930→#### Test: Assignee filter allows multi-select\n   931→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues assigned to Alice (2), Bob (1), Charlie (1)\n   932→- **Action**: User opens Assignee filter, checks \"Alice\" and \"Bob\"\n   933→- **Expected**: Issues assigned to Alice and Bob are shown. Charlie's issues are hidden. The filter button indicates 2 assignees selected.\n   934→\n   935→## Issue Detail Page (`/issue/:issueId`)\n   936→\n   937→**Components**: IssueHeader, IssueDescription, SubIssues, ActivityComments, IssueSidebar\n   938→\n   939→### IssueHeader\n   940→\n   941→#### Test: Issue header renders identifier and title\n   942→- **Initial state**: User navigates to `/issue/:issueId` for an existing issue with identifier \"ENG-42\" and title \"Fix login bug\"\n   943→- **Expected**: The header displays the issue identifier \"ENG-42\" and the title \"Fix login bug\" in large font. The identifier is non-editable. The status selector is visible below the title showing the current status with its icon and color.\n   944→\n   945→#### Test: Inline edit issue title\n   946→- **Initial state**: User is on the issue detail page for issue \"ENG-42\" with title \"Fix login bug\"\n   947→- **Action**: User clicks on the title text \"Fix login bug\"\n   948→- **Expected**: The title becomes an editable text input pre-filled with \"Fix login bug\". The input is focused and ready for editing.\n   949→\n   950→#### Test: Save edited issue title\n   951→- **Initial state**: User has clicked the title and it is in edit mode, showing \"Fix login bug\"\n   952→- **Action**: User clears the field, types \"Fix authentication bug\", and presses Enter (or clicks away to blur)\n   953→- **Expected**: The title updates to \"Fix authentication bug\". The change is persisted to the database. The title returns to display mode. An activity entry is created recording the title change.\n   954→\n   955→#### Test: Cancel title edit on Escape\n   956→- **Initial state**: User has clicked the title and it is in edit mode, showing \"Fix login bug\"\n   957→- **Action**: User types some characters, then presses Escape\n   958→- **Expected**: The title reverts to the original \"Fix login bug\" without saving. The field returns to display mode.\n   959→\n   960→#### Test: Title edit validates non-empty\n   961→- **Initial state**: User has clicked the title and it is in edit mode\n   962→- **Action**: User clears the title field completely and presses Enter\n   963→- **Expected**: A validation error is shown (e.g., red border or tooltip) indicating the title cannot be empty. The original title is preserved.\n   964→\n   965→#### Test: Inline status selector displays current status\n   966→- **Initial state**: User is on the issue detail page for an issue with status \"In Progress\"\n   967→- **Expected**: The status selector below the title shows a half-circle icon in yellow and the text \"In Progress\".\n   968→\n   969→#### Test: Change status via inline selector\n   970→- **Initial state**: User is on the issue detail page for an issue with status \"Todo\"\n   971→- **Action**: User clicks the status selector\n   972→- **Expected**: A dropdown appears showing all statuses (Backlog, Todo, In Progress, In Review, Done, Cancelled) each with their respective icon and color.\n   973→\n   974→#### Test: Select new status from dropdown\n   975→- **Initial state**: The status dropdown is open, current status is \"Todo\"\n   976→- **Action**: User clicks \"In Progress\" in the dropdown\n   977→- **Expected**: The dropdown closes. The status selector updates to show the half-circle icon in yellow with text \"In Progress\". The change is persisted to the database. An activity entry is created recording the status change from \"Todo\" to \"In Progress\". A notification is created for subscribers of this issue.\n   978→\n   979→#### Test: Status dropdown closes on outside click\n   980→- **Initial state**: The status dropdown is open\n   981→- **Action**: User clicks outside the dropdown\n   982→- **Expected**: The dropdown closes without changing the status.\n   983→\n   984→#### Test: Issue detail page shows correct layout with left and right panels\n   985→- **Initial state**: User navigates to `/issue/:issueId` for an existing issue\n   986→- **Expected**: The page displays a two-panel layout: the left panel (~70% width) contains the issue header, description, sub-issues, and activity/comments sections. The right panel (~30% width) contains the sidebar with issue properties.\n   987→\n   988→### IssueDescription\n   989→\n   990→#### Test: Description renders markdown content\n   991→- **Initial state**: User is on the issue detail page for an issue with a markdown description containing headings, bold text, code blocks, and bullet lists\n   992→- **Expected**: The description area renders the markdown as formatted HTML — headings are styled, bold text is bold, code blocks have monospace font with background, and bullet lists are properly indented.\n   993→\n   994→#### Test: Description shows placeholder when empty\n   995→- **Initial state**: User is on the issue detail page for an issue with no description\n   996→- **Expected**: The description area shows a placeholder text (e.g., \"Add a description...\") in muted/gray text, indicating it is clickable to add content.\n   997→\n   998→#### Test: Click to edit description\n   999→- **Initial state**: User is on the issue detail page with a description \"This is a bug in the login flow\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01WjMpzpkaoonEAv4tNVAEdb","session_id":"cea1a0db-f072-4eb0-98ad-c0869b93e80c","uuid":"24d4b50d-300f-4f88-91ea-c4b164319334"}
